# VEYR House Architecture
VEYR is structured as four interoperable houses.
                 VEYR
                  │
        ┌─────────┼─────────┬──────────┐
        │         │         │          │
      STUDIO    SYSTEMS   OBJECTS   PRODUCTION
        │         │         │          │
        └─────────┴────┬────┴──────────┘
                       │
                    CULTURE
VEYR does not assume a project belongs permanently to one division.
Projects move.
---
# Core Pipeline
RAW INTENT
↓
CONTEXT EXTRACTION
↓
INVARIANT / DESIRE
↓
CULTURAL + FUNCTIONAL RESEARCH
↓
DESIGN SPACE GENERATION
↓
VEYR REDUCTION
↓
SYSTEM / FORM SELECTION
↓
PROTOTYPE
↓
CRITIQUE
↓
REFINEMENT
↓
PRODUCTION
↓
OBSERVATION
↓
HOUSE MEMORY
---
# VEYR Reduction
Pantheon-style exploration may generate many valid forms.
VEYR deliberately destroys most of them.
VEYR_REDuce(options):
    preserve:
        strongest underlying idea
        emotional target
        functional requirement
        contextual fit
        surprising useful detail
    eliminate:
        explanation
        redundant symbolism
        unnecessary controls
        performative complexity
        imitation
        visual noise
    return:
        smallest artifact capable of carrying the full intention
Reduction is not simplification for its own sake.
It is compression without semantic loss.
---
# Project Routing
IF problem is primarily:
    identity / taste / narrative / aesthetic
THEN route → STUDIO
IF problem is primarily:
    intelligence / software / adaptation / interface
THEN route → SYSTEMS
IF problem requires:
    physical embodiment / manufacture / material
THEN route → OBJECTS
IF problem requires:
    public execution / campaign / media / launch
THEN route → PRODUCTION
IF multiple:
    create cross-house project cell
Cross-house work is expected.

